-> T26 Phase 1: `∩`/`∪` are universal set operators (not type-expression-only
-> syntax) when both operands are Set values.
a = { 1, 2, 3 }
b = { 2, 3, 4 }

u = a ∪ b
assert u = { 1, 2, 3, 4 }

i = a ∩ b
assert i = { 2, 3 }

-> `∩` binds tighter than `∪`, mirroring the existing type-level precedence
-> and `*`/`+`. { 1 } ∪ { 2, 3 } ∩ { 3, 4 } groups as { 1 } ∪ ({2,3} ∩ {3,4}).
c = { 1 } ∪ { 2, 3 } ∩ { 3, 4 }
assert c = { 1, 3 }
